  "contracts": {
    "json": "Keep Unicode control spelling including lowercase \\u0008/\\u000c; ordinary UTF-8 and object/number representation stay with the existing consumer adapter. Writer constructor and Unicode policy references are checked; receiver dataflow remains a behavior-review concern.",
    "windows": "Keep read-only owner/DACL checks, DACL-only reprotection, owner initialization only for new objects; GUI uses ObjectOnly, daemon and installer use FilesAndDirectories. The removed protect_created bodies perform a native owner write and the protection/validation sequence; the new forwarding wrappers are retained.",
    "indirect_routes": "zuse platform forwards to src/json.rs. Installer private.rs includes ../../../src/privacy_windows.rs. The registered reference_path supplies lexical provider evidence while the entry path determines its owning Cargo package; these records do not resolve a Rust module graph.",
    "retained": "Do not replace original parsers or their hex4/hex_quad error/capacity contracts. SSMCP accepts TokenOwner and has different DACL inheritance/count/presence rules; its current/verify_private functions are negative fixtures. Token-buffer helpers and BCrypt randomness are outside the removed ACL body inventory."
  }
